  "description": "A series of conical tumuli near the Iranian village of Cheshm\u00e9 G\u00f6l. The tumuli were initially identified by Sir Aurel Stein in 1936. They were subsequently investigated by Oscar White Muscarella. The site is located some 5 km east of Dinkha Tepe in the Ushnu valley.",
